inPassage":3,"uses":42},{"base":"H6240","lemma":"עָשָׂר","tr":"a·sar","gloss":"ten","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":337},{"base":"H8269","lemma":"שַׂר","tr":"sar","gloss":"ruler","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":421},{"base":"H2227","lemma":"זַרְחִי","tr":"zar·chi","gloss":"Zerahite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H7223","lemma":"רִאשׁוֹן","tr":"ri·shon","gloss":"first","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":181}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":21,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Some time later at Gob, there was another battle with the Philistines. At that time Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Saph, one of the descendants of Rapha.","from":11},{"book":"2SA","chapter":23,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"These are the names of Davidʼs mighty men: Josheb-basshebeth the Tahchemonite was chief of the Three. He wielded his spear against eight hundred men, whom he killed at one time.","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This is the list of Davidʼs mighty men: Jashobeam son of Hachmoni was chief of the officers; he wielded his spear against three hundred men, whom he killed at one time.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":38,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But when he pulled his hand back and his brother came out, she said, “You have broken out first!” So he was named Perez.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":8,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Judah, your brothers shall praise you. Your hand shall be on the necks of your enemies; your fatherʼs sons shall bow down to you. Judah is a young lion— my son, you return from the prey. Like a lion he crouches and lies down; like a lioness, who dares to rouse him? The scepter will not depart from Judah, nor the staff from between his feet, until Shiloh comes and the allegiance of the nations is his.","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Moses chose capable men from all Israel and made them heads over the people as leaders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens.","from":1},{"book":"NUM","chapter":7,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On the first day Nahshon son of Amminadab from the tribe of Judah drew near with his offering.","from":3},{"book":"NUM","chapter":10,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"First, the divisions of the camp of Judah set out under their standard, with Nahshon son of Amminadab in command.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"16-24":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"eliezer-h0461k","name":"Eliezer","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zichri","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"maacah-h4601p","name":"Maacah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Shephatiah","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"shephatiah-h8203j","name":"Shephatiah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Maacah","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"zichri-h2147m","name":"Zichri","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Eliezer","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"hashabiah-h2811k","name":"Hashabiah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Kemuel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"kemuel-h7055i","name":"Kemuel","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Hashabiah","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son 