460","lemma":"יִשְׁמַעְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"yish·ma·yah","gloss":"Ishmaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5812","lemma":"עֲזַזְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"a·zaz·ya·hu","gloss":"Azaziah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5837","lemma":"עַזְרִיאֵל","tr":"az·ri·el","gloss":"Azriel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And the Lordtook him outside and said, “Now look to the heavens and count the stars, if you are able.” Then He told him, “So shall your offspring be.”","from":23},{"book":"NUM","chapter":1,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and on the first day of the second month they assembled the whole congregation and recorded their ancestry by clans and families, counting one by one the names of those twenty years of age or older,","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":14,"verse":50,"verseEnd":51,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"His wifeʼs name was Ahinoam daughter of Ahimaaz. The name of the commander of his army was Abner, the son of Saulʼs uncle Ner. Saulʼs father Kish and Abnerʼs father Ner were sons of Abiel.","from":21},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When they arrived, Samuel saw Eliab and said, “Surely here before the LORD is His anointed.”","from":18},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The three older sons of Jesse had followed Saul into battle: The firstborn was Eliab, the second was Abinadab, and the third was Shammah.","from":18},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“What have I done now?” said David. “Was it not just a question?”","from":18},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Abner returned to Hebron, Joab pulled him aside into the gateway, as if to speak to him privately, and there Joab stabbed him in the stomach. So Abner died on account of the blood of Joabʼs brother Asahel.","from":21},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So on that day all the troops and all Israel were convinced that the king had no part in the murder of Abner son of Ner.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":9},{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"25-31":{"people":[{"id":"adiel-h5717i","name":"Adiel","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Azmaveth","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"azmaveth-h5820j","name":"Azmaveth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adiel","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"jonathan-h3083k","name":"Jonathan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Uzziah","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"uzziah-h5818i","name":"Uzziah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jonathan","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"chelub-h3620h","name":"Chelub","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Ezri","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ezri-h5836","name":"Ezri","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Chelub","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ramathites-h7435","name":"Ramathites","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"shimei-h8096o","name":"Shimei","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"shiphmites-h8225","name":"Shiphmites","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"zabdi-h2067i","name":"Zabdi","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"baal-hanan-h1177h","name":"Baal-hanan","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"joash-h3135h","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"adlai-h5724","name":"Adlai","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Shaphat","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"shaphat-h8202k","name":"Shaphat","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adlai","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"shitrai-h