ge":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3723","lemma":"כָּפָר","tr":"ka·phar","gloss":"Chephar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":41,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"During those seven years, Joseph collected all the excess food in the land of Egypt and stored it in the cities. In every city he laid up the food from the fields around it.","from":25},{"book":"GEN","chapter":47,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the land of Egypt is before you; settle your father and brothers in the best part of the land. They may dwell in the land of Goshen. And if you know of any talented men among them, put them in charge of my own livestock.”","from":30},{"book":"EXO","chapter":1,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So the Egyptians appointed taskmasters over the Israelites to oppress them with forced labor. As a result, they built Pithom and Rameses as store cities for Pharaoh.","from":25},{"book":"1KI","chapter":4,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Solomon had twelve governors over all Israel to provide food for the king and his household. Each one would arrange provisions for one month of the year,","from":28},{"book":"1KI","chapter":20,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Israelites also mobilized, gathered supplies, and marched out to meet them. The Israelites camped before them like two small flocks of goats, while the Arameans covered the countryside.","from":28},{"book":"2KI","chapter":18,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Hezekiah gave him all the silver that was found in the house of the LORD and in the treasuries of the royal palace.","from":25},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and its towns, and throughout the pasturelands of Sharon.","from":29},{"book":"2CH","chapter":16,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Asa withdrew the silver and gold from the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he sent it with this message to Ben-hadad king of Aram, who was ruling in Damascus:","from":25}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"32-34":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"hachmoni-h2453h","name":"Hachmoni","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"jehiel-h3171i","name":"Jehiel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hachmoni","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"jonadab-h3122g","name":"Jonadab","kind":"person","brief":"David's nephew","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"ahithophel-h0302","name":"Ahithophel","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":2,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"archites-h0757","name":"Archites","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"hushai-h2365","name":"Hushai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"abiathar-h0054","name":"Abiathar","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"benaiah-h1141k","name":"Benaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jehoiada","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"jehoiada-h3077i","name":"Jehoiada","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Benaiah","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":34}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0302","lemma":"אֲחִיתֹ֫פֶל","tr":"a·chi·to·phel","gloss":"Ahithophel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H3289","lemma":"יָעַץ","tr":"ya·ats","gloss":"to advise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":79},{"base":"H2453","lemma":"חַכְמוֹנִי","tr":"chakh·mo·ni","gloss":"Hachmonite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0757","lemma":"אַרְכִּי","tr":"ar·ki","gloss":"Archite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H2365","lemma":"חוּשַׁי","tr":"chu·shay","gloss":"Hushai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H3171","lemma":"יְחִיאֵל","tr":"ye·chi·el","gloss":"Jehiel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H0054","lemma":"אֶבְיָתָר","tr":"ev·ya·tar","gloss":"Abiathar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H1141","lemma":"בְּנָיָ֫הוּ","tr":"be·na·yah","gloss":"Benaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":42},{"base":"H3077","lemma":"יְהוֹיָדָע","tr":"ye·ho·ya·da","gloss":"Jehoiada","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":51},{"base":"H1730","lemma":"דּוֹד","tr":"dod","gloss":"beloved","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":61}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"While Absalom was offering the sacrifices, he sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, Davidʼs counselor, to come from his hometown of Giloh. So the conspiracy gained strength, and Absalomʼs following kept increasing.","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Davidʼs friend Hushai arrived in Jerusalem just as Absalom was entering the city.","from":33},{"book":"1KI","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Adonijah conferred with Joab son of Zeruiah and with Abiathar the priest, who supported him.","from":34},{"book":"1CH","chapter":11,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now David had said, “Whoever is the first to strike down a Jebusite will become chief commander.” And Joab son of Zeruiah went up first, and he became the chief.","from":34},{"book":"2SA","chapter":13,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now Amnon had a friend named Jonadab, the son of Davidʼs brother Shimeah. Jonadab was a very shrewd man,","from":32},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When David came to the summit, where he used to worship God, Hushai the Archite was there to meet him with his robe torn and dust on his head.","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":16,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Davidʼs friend Hushai the Archite went to Absalom and said to him, “Long live the king! Long live the king!”","from":33},{"book":"2SA","chapter":16,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Is this the loyalty you show your friend?” Absalom replied. “Why did you not go with your friend?”","from":33}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":5}]}}